Subject: [PATCH] Autosave the level data and the global saved data

MinecraftServer#tickServer is only called with a region (from
TickRegions), so its "region == null" branch, the only place that called
saveGlobalData and saveIncrementally(true) on the autosave interval, never
runs. The clock and weather state, game rules, scoreboard and teams, world
border, raids, the dragon fight, forced chunks, the map index and the
level.dat of every world were only written by a clean stop or a save-all,
so a crash lost all of it since the last of those.

Every ticks-per.autosave the global region now writes the global saved
data and each world's level data, honouring save-off and each world's
noSave, and fires WorldSaveEvent. This is the work vanilla does on the
main thread, done on the thread that owns that data. Players and chunks
are still saved by their own regions as before.

diff --git a/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java b/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java
index aa575f3b76ef70ffb9f0410e7e5cfe7af384bfbd..0944c32fcb0b838f80a8b243f418fb28fde24c4c 100644
--- a/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java
+++ b/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java
@@ -230,6 +230,7 @@ public final class RegionizedServer {
 
     private long lastServerStatus;
     private long tickCount;
+    private long lastGlobalDataAutoSaveTick; // Folia - save the level data and the global saved data
 
     private void globalTick(final long tickCount) {
         ++this.tickCount;
@@ -264,7 +265,28 @@ public final class RegionizedServer {
 
         // player list
         MinecraftServer.getServer().getPlayerList().tick();
+
+        // auto save of the level data and the global saved data
+        this.autoSaveGlobalData(); // Folia - save the level data and the global saved data
+    }
+
+    // Folia start - save the level data and the global saved data
+    private void autoSaveGlobalData() {
+        final MinecraftServer server = MinecraftServer.getServer();
+        final int autoSavePeriod = server.autosavePeriod;
+        if (autoSavePeriod <= 0 || !server.isAutoSave() || (this.tickCount - this.lastGlobalDataAutoSaveTick) < (long)autoSavePeriod) {
+            return;
+        }
+        this.lastGlobalDataAutoSaveTick = this.tickCount;
+
+        server.saveGlobalData(false);
+        for (final ServerLevel world : this.worlds) {
+            if (world.paperConfig().chunks.autoSaveInterval.value() > 0 && !world.noSave) {
+                world.saveIncrementally(true);
+            }
+        }
     }
+    // Folia end - save the level data and the global saved data
 
     private void tickPlayerSample() {
         final MinecraftServer mcServer = MinecraftServer.getServer();
